  "content": {
    "id": "p44-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find the number of arrangements of the letters of the word BRIMSTONE if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$9!=362\\,880$",
          "worked": "All nine letters are distinct.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=9!\\\\N&=362\\,880\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the vowels are all together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$30\\,240$ arrangements.\n\nTreat I, O and E as one block; arrange the seven objects and the three vowels within their block.",
          "worked": "Treat I, O and E as one block. The block and six consonants form seven distinct objects. The vowels have $3!$ internal orders.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=7!\\times3!\\\\N&=30\\,240\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "no two of the letters B, I and T are adjacent.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$151\\,200$ arrangements.\n\nArrange the other six letters, then place B, I and T in three different gaps.",
          "worked": "Arrange R, M, S, O, N and E in $6!$ ways. There are seven gaps, including the two ends. Place B, I and T in different gaps, giving $7$, $6$ and $5$ choices respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=6!\\times7\\times6\\times5\\\\N&=151\\,200\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
